@* The trigger stays a real link: a hover card previews what the link points at, and the link
   has to work for everyone who never hovers — touch, keyboard, screen reader. The pointer may
   travel from the trigger into the panel without it closing, which is the one thing that makes
   a hover card usable and the one thing implementations forget. *@
<HoverCard>
    <HoverCardTrigger Target="demo-hc" Href="/components/avatar" Class="underline underline-offset-4">
        @@marta
    </HoverCardTrigger>
    <HoverCardContent Id="demo-hc" Class="w-72 p-4">
        <div class="flex gap-3">
            <Avatar><AvatarFallback>MR</AvatarFallback></Avatar>
            <div class="space-y-1">
                <p class="text-sm font-medium">Marta Ruiz</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Joined March 2024 · 128 orders</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </HoverCardContent>
</HoverCard>
